# InputComponents — authored components that say which node CONSUMES an input
# channel. Input is routed once per frame by `updateUiInput`
# (ui/inputSystem): the channel goes to exactly one consumer, and systems ask
# for their share by identity (`uiWheelFor`) instead of reading the device.

# Marks a node that takes the scroll wheel while the pointer is over it: a
# canvas that zooms, a viewport that pans. A `ScrollRoot` is a wheel consumer
# without this tag. The wheel goes to the nearest consumer on the path to the
# topmost node under the pointer, so a list scrolling inside a panel does not
# also zoom the canvas beside or behind it.
#
#     "Canvas": { "WheelTarget": {} }
type WheelTarget {
}
